  "title": "Italy's Electoral Reform Approved Amid Opposition Criticism",
  "summary": "The Italian government approved an electoral overhaul that aims to improve political stability by introducing a fully proportional system, with opposition parties accusing the move of strengthening the power of a particular political figure, Giorgia Meloni, while critics argue the system disproportionately benefits those who support her.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Italian parliament approved a fully proportional electoral reform that introduces bonus seats for coalitions winning the most votes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Opposition parties have criticized the reform, arguing it disproportionately benefits those in power, including Giorgia Meloni.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reform was finalized in a secret ballot process, with public approval from the Italian government.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
